; voice-track-worker-run.fk — one tongue's pieces, rendered by the body's own mouth from the body's own tables.
; The tongue is named in .hearth/voice-track/worker.request (the supervisor writes it). Resumable.
; Proof: the 2026-10-03 run of all four tongues (receipts/2026-10-03-the-voice-spoke-without-leaving-the-body.md); no band reads this cell yet.
; The worker holds the GPU lease (/tmp/form-gpu.lock, machine-wide, gpu-lease.bml) for its run -- vtr-leased-work -- and the supervisor
; (voice-track.bml) does not: a worker the supervisor kills leaves a dead owner's lease, and the next worker takes it over.
; preludes: form/form-stdlib/voice-track.bml
(do
    (let code (trim (read_file ".hearth/voice-track/worker.request")))
    (vtr-leased-work code)
    0)
